Sval: Remove Normandy

Normandy is Mozilla's recipe client for preference studies, add-on
studies and Heartbeat surveys. Sval locks studies off and points it at no
server, so it only ran its startup and shutdown work. It goes with its
about:studies actor, its extension API, the DisableFirefoxStudies policy,
its prefs and its tests. Normandy started Nimbus once the session's
windows were restored; BrowserGlue starts it there instead, and
FirstStartup waits for Nimbus directly. Nimbus and targeting take the
randomization id from ClientEnvironmentBase. Normandy's metrics.yaml
stays: Nimbus records its enrollment events under that category.

